# Node.js (Nest) service structure

Use this layout for Channels, Notifications, and other Nest services:

```
src/
├── server.ts                 # bootstrap listen()
├── app/
│   ├── app.module.ts         # composition root (Nest module)
│   ├── config.ts             # env / ports / downstream URLs
│   └── middleware/           # Nest middleware / filters (optional)
│
├── features/
│   └── {area}/
│       ├── {area}.types.ts   # or {area}.domain.ts for area DTOs/commands
│       └── {use-case}/
│           ├── route.ts      # HTTP controller (Nest @Controller)
│           ├── schema.ts     # input validation / DTO
│           ├── handler.ts    # CQRS command/query handler
│           └── service.ts    # optional orchestration (call infra/domain)
│
├── domain/
│   ├── {bounded-context}/
│   └── shared/
│
├── infrastructure/
│   ├── database/             # JSON/SQLite/Prisma when the spec requires it
│   ├── http/                 # outbound clients to other CRM services
│   ├── cache/                # only when the spec names a cache
│   ├── messaging/            # only when the spec names a broker
│   ├── email/
│   └── storage/
│
└── shared/
    ├── errors/
    ├── result/
    ├── logger/
    ├── utils/
    └── types/
```

## Nest naming map

| File | Nest role |
|---|---|
| `route.ts` | `@Controller` — maps HTTP; no business rules |
| `schema.ts` | request DTO + validation helpers |
| `handler.ts` | `@CommandHandler` / `@QueryHandler` |
| `service.ts` | injectable use-case helper when handler would be too thick |

## Rules

1. **Composition only** in `app/` + `server.ts` — no feature HTTP handlers there.
2. One use-case folder = one HTTP surface (or a tightly related pair).
3. Domain types stay in `domain/`; feature `*.types.ts` holds transport/use-case DTOs.
4. Persistence and outbound HTTP live under `infrastructure/`, not inside `features/`.
5. Keep CQRS (`@nestjs/cqrs`) for writes/reads.
6. **Do not** add Redis, RabbitMQ, Prisma, or S3 unless the active spec names them — folders may exist as empty placeholders only when useful.
7. JSON/SQLite local persistence remains the default for demos.
8. Cite `CRM-nnn` in new feature file headers.
